{"id":"b3f55351a8a5176d","group":"58","path":"58/batch11/58-df-curve.md","title":"Algebraic Curve","display":"df-curve — Algebraic Curve","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-curve","aliases":["58-df-curve","Algebraic Curve"],"display":"df-curve — Algebraic Curve","depends_on":["[[../batch19/58-df-polynomial.md]]","[[../batch12/58-df-irreducible.md]]","[[../batch13/58-df-field.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-curve"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-curve</span><span>Algebraic Curve</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-curve — Algebraic Curve"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ab5e359a8ea0dcb4\" href=\"?note=ab5e359a8ea0dcb4\" title=\"../batch19/58-df-polynomial.md\">../batch19/58-df-polynomial.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"8c958034cb5b5a95\" href=\"?note=8c958034cb5b5a95\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-irreducible.md\">../batch12/58-df-irreducible.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"1eb4a89b005d9cda\" href=\"?note=1eb4a89b005d9cda\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-field.md\">../batch13/58-df-field.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k,+_k,\\cdot_k,0_k,1_k\">\\(k,+_k,\\cdot_k,0_k,1_k\\)</span> (algebraically closed field datum)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P_k\\coloneqq(k^3\\setminus\\{0\\})/{\\sim_k}\">\\(P_k\\coloneqq(k^3\\setminus\\{0\\})/{\\sim_k}\\)</span>, where <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"u\\sim_kv\\leftrightarrow\\exists\\lambda\\in k\\setminus\\{0_k\\}\\;(v=\\lambda\\cdot_k u)\">\\(u\\sim_kv\\leftrightarrow\\exists\\lambda\\in k\\setminus\\{0_k\\}\\;(v=\\lambda\\cdot_k u)\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R_k\\coloneqq k[x,y,z]\">\\(R_k\\coloneqq k[x,y,z]\\)</span> with induced operations <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R\">\\(+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R\\)</span>, and homogeneous pieces <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(R_{k,d})_{d&gt;0}\">\\((R_{k,d})_{d&gt;0}\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"C\\subseteq P_k\">\\(C\\subseteq P_k\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"0_R\\neq f\\in R_k\">\\(0_R\\neq f\\in R_k\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Field}_S,\\mathrm{Irreducible}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Field}_S,\\mathrm{Irreducible}_S\\)</span> (field and irreducible-element predicates from dependencies)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PlaneCurve}_S,\\mathrm{SmoothCurve}_S\\subseteq V^7\">\\(\\mathrm{PlaneCurve}_S,\\mathrm{SmoothCurve}_S\\subseteq V^7\\)</span> (predicates defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PlaneCurveGenus}_S\\subseteq V^8\">\\(\\mathrm{PlaneCurveGenus}_S\\subseteq V^8\\)</span> (plane-curve genus predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}curve\\text{-}plane} \\vdash \\mathrm{PlaneCurve}_S(C,f,k,+_k,\\cdot_k,0_k,1_k)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Field}_S(k,+_k,\\cdot_k,0_k,1_k)\\land\\bigl(\\forall q\\in k[t]\\setminus k\\;\\exists a\\in k\\;(q(a)=0_k)\\bigr)\\land\\exists d\\in\\mathbb N_{&gt;0}\\;(f\\in R_{k,d})\\land\\mathrm{Irreducible}_S\\bigl(f;R_k,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R\\bigr)\\land C=\\{p\\in P_k:f(p)=0_k\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}curve\\text{-}plane} \\vdash \\mathrm{PlaneCurve}_S(C,f,k,+_k,\\cdot_k,0_k,1_k)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Field}_S(k,+_k,\\cdot_k,0_k,1_k)\\land\\bigl(\\forall q\\in k[t]\\setminus k\\;\\exists a\\in k\\;(q(a)=0_k)\\bigr)\\land\\exists d\\in\\mathbb N_{&gt;0}\\;(f\\in R_{k,d})\\land\\mathrm{Irreducible}_S\\bigl(f;R_k,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R\\bigr)\\land C=\\{p\\in P_k:f(p)=0_k\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}curve\\text{-}smooth} \\vdash \\mathrm{SmoothCurve}_S(C,f,k,+_k,\\cdot_k,0_k,1_k)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{PlaneCurve}_S(C,f,k,+_k,\\cdot_k,0_k,1_k)\\land\\forall p\\in C\\;\\bigl((\\partial_xf(p),\\partial_yf(p),\\partial_zf(p))\\neq(0_k,0_k,0_k)\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}curve\\text{-}smooth} \\vdash \\mathrm{SmoothCurve}_S(C,f,k,+_k,\\cdot_k,0_k,1_k)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{PlaneCurve}_S(C,f,k,+_k,\\cdot_k,0_k,1_k)\\land\\forall p\\in C\\;\\bigl((\\partial_xf(p),\\partial_yf(p),\\partial_zf(p))\\neq(0_k,0_k,0_k)\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}curve\\text{-}genus} \\vdash \\mathrm{PlaneCurveGenus}_S(g,C,f,k,+_k,\\cdot_k,0_k,1_k)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{SmoothCurve}_S(C,f,k,+_k,\\cdot_k,0_k,1_k)\\land g=\\frac{(\\deg(f)-1)(\\deg(f)-2)}{2}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}curve\\text{-}genus} \\vdash \\mathrm{PlaneCurveGenus}_S(g,C,f,k,+_k,\\cdot_k,0_k,1_k)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{SmoothCurve}_S(C,f,k,+_k,\\cdot_k,0_k,1_k)\\land g=\\frac{(\\deg(f)-1)(\\deg(f)-2)}{2}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Algebraic curve: 1-dimensional integral scheme of finite type over <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k\">\\(k\\)</span></li>\n<li>The displayed genus formula is restricted to smooth projective plane curves; it is false without singularity corrections for arbitrary plane curves.</li>\n<li>The projective plane is built from the chosen field multiplication; it does not reuse the narrower upstream atom that only defines real and complex projective spaces.</li>\n<li>Homogeneity is expressed by membership in a positive-degree graded piece of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R_k\">\\(R_k\\)</span>, and irreducibility is evaluated in that polynomial ring with the upstream predicate's full signature.</li>\n<li>Genus <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"g = 0\">\\(g = 0\\)</span>: rational curves (<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{P}^1\">\\(\\mathbb{P}^1\\)</span>); <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"g = 1\">\\(g = 1\\)</span>: elliptic curves</li>\n<li>Riemann-Roch: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\ell(D) - \\ell(K-D) = \\deg(D) - g + 1\">\\(\\ell(D) - \\ell(K-D) = \\deg(D) - g + 1\\)</span></li>\n<li>Birational classification: curves of genus <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\geq 2\">\\(\\geq 2\\)</span> are hyperelliptic or generic</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Hartshorne, Algebraic Geometry</li>\n<li>Fulton, Algebraic Curves</li>\n<li>Miranda, Algebraic Curves and Riemann Surfaces</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch19/58-df-polynomial.md","status":"resolved","id":"ab5e359a8ea0dcb4","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch19/58-df-polynomial.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch12/58-df-irreducible.md","status":"resolved","id":"8c958034cb5b5a95","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-df-irreducible.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch13/58-df-field.md","status":"resolved","id":"1eb4a89b005d9cd